22:["$","$L28","3",{"block":{"type":"drag-drop","mode":"match","title":"Pick the permission","prompt":"Drag the permission each person needs onto their situation.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Andre needs to see what each showing is and where, but shouldn't change them.","match":"See event details"},{"id":"b","text":"Kim moves and adds showings when repairs run long.","match":"Make changes and see event details"},{"id":"c","text":"A vendor only needs to know when the office is busy.","match":"See only free/busy (hide details)"},{"id":"d","text":"Denise, as office manager, decides who else gets access.","match":"Make changes and manage sharing"}],"explanation":"Give each person the least access that lets them do their job. You can always raise it later."}}]
23:["$","div","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Public calendars"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"In Settings and sharing, under Access permissions for events, Make available to public lets anyone see the calendar, including through Google search. That suits something like a community room's open hours. It doesn't suit a calendar with tenants' names, unit numbers, or anyone's personal appointments."}],["$","div","1",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Never make a calendar public if it holds names, addresses, phone numbers, or other personal details. Share it with specific people instead."]}]]}]]}]
24:["$","div","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Appointment schedules"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"An appointment schedule offers open times that other people book on a booking page, so nobody has to email back and forth. You can create one with a personal Google Account or a Google Workspace account on a computer (not in the Calendar phone app). Some features need an eligible Google Workspace or Google One subscription, and a work account's administrator may need to turn it on."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Select Create, then Appointment schedule."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"In the Bookable appointment schedule panel, add a title and choose the Appointment duration."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Under General availability, set the days and hours you're available each week."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Optionally set the Scheduling window (how far ahead people can book; the shortest notice is 4 hours by default) and Booked appointment settings such as buffer time and a daily limit."}],["$","li","4",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Select Next. Choose the location or video conferencing, add a description, and set up the booking form. First name, last name, and email are always required; you can add items such as a phone number and require email verification."}],["$","li","5",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Select Save."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"To share it, find it under Booking pages on the left side of Calendar, point to it, and select Copy link. Paste the link into an email or your website. A booking page is always public: anyone with the link can see the booking page, your profile photo, and your account name."}],["$","div","3",{"className":"bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-400 p-4 rounded-xl text-gray-800 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡 "}],"Give the schedule a title tenants will understand, such as “Tenant office hours”, and keep the description short: what the call is for and what to have ready."]}]]}]]}]
25:["$","div","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Knowledge Check"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","$L29","0",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A coworker should be able to add events to your calendar but not share it with anyone else. Which permission?","options":["See only free/busy (hide details)","See event details","Make changes and see event details","Make changes and manage sharing"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Make changes and see event details lets them edit events; only manage sharing lets them share the calendar.","optionRationales":["They couldn't add events.","They could only look.","Correct.","That would let them share the calendar too."]}}],["$","$L29","1",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Who can see your appointment schedule's booking page?","options":["Only people in your organization","Anyone who has the link","Only your Contacts","Nobody until you approve them"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Booking pages are always public. Anyone with the link sees the page, your profile photo, and your account name.","optionRationales":["Booking pages aren't limited to your organization.","Correct.","There's no Contacts-only option.","People book directly from the page."]}}]]}]]}]
